      "question": "At the end of the handover, how does the incoming caregiver confirm they have received and understood all the information — for example, do they sign off on a list, send a message, or is it purely verbal?",
      "answer": "The incoming caregiver explicitly acknowledges the remaining tasks. If acknowledgement has not been given, the outgoing caregiver confirms directly before leaving tasks assigned. The specific mechanism — verbal, message, or sign-off — is not specified beyond this acknowledged confirmation step."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q2",
      "question": "Can you walk me through the specific tasks that make up 'getting things ready for the next day' — for instance, what is typically packed, prepared, or checked before the evening ends?",
      "answer": "The partner prepares items needed for the next day guided by the next-day schedule, then marks completed preparation tasks in a checklist. Any unresolved preparation items are left open and the responsible owner is contacted. The specific physical items packed or checked are not specified."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q3",
      "question": "Is any tool currently used to record or share handover information — such as a shared notes app, a whiteboard, a messaging thread, or a printed sheet?",
      "answer": "Yes. A family handover log records handover information, an evening task checklist tracks preparation tasks, a shared family calendar holds schedule information, and a family messaging app supports communication. Only participating caregivers can read the shared log, and task completion is recorded manually."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q4",
      "question": "How do you decide which tasks or updates are important enough to include in the handover — is there a fixed set of topics you always cover, or does it depend on what happened that day?",
      "answer": "The handover covers unfinished household care tasks from the day and the next-day schedule. Caregiver notes relevant to the incoming caregiver are also shared. Any conflicting or missing task information is clarified. Whether the scope is a fixed template or varies by day is not specified."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q5",
      "question": "What happens when the incoming caregiver is not available at the expected time — how is the handover information preserved or communicated in that situation?",
      "answer": "Incoming caregiver unavailability is listed as a recognised exception. Unresolved tasks are left open and the responsible owner is contacted, and a tool can send reminders about unresolved tasks. However, the detailed fallback procedure for a fully absent incoming caregiver is not specified."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q6",
      "question": "How many evenings per week does this handover routine take place, and does the schedule change depending on the day of the week or other family commitments?",
      "answer": "The handover takes place each evening when care responsibility changes in the household. The exact number of evenings per week and whether the schedule varies by day or family commitments are not specified."
    }
  ]
}
